{
    "$schema": "https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json",
    "description": "Keeps every pinned version current: base images, the k3s release of kubeenv, application images' upstream releases, build tools, GitHub Actions. Base images are pinned to a major release, not a digest: the weekly rebuild (build-bootc.yml) picks up their updates within it.",
    "extends": ["github>spnngl/.github:renovate.default.json5"],
    // Digests for actions and the application images' FROM lines only: the
    // preset's config:best-practices pins every image, and a digest on a
    // bootc Containerfile's FROM would freeze the base between rebuilds (see
    // the pinDigests rule below).
    "ignorePresets": ["docker:pinDigests"],
    // Any time; the Debian snapshot rules below wait for Saturday,
    // midnight to 5am, the day before the weekly rebuild.
    "schedule": ["at any time"],
    "automergeSchedule": ["at any time"],
    // dockerfile: the application images' FROM lines.
    // custom.regex: every other version, written once each in a docker-bake.hcl
    // (containers/AGENTS.md, bootc/AGENTS.md).
    "enabledManagers": ["dockerfile", "github-actions", "custom.regex"],
    // Debian's archive snapshots (snapshot.debian.org), newest 300: its JSON
    // is {"result": {"debian": [<timestamp>...]}}, all of them, oldest first.
    "customDatasources": {
        "debian-snapshot": {
            "defaultRegistryUrlTemplate": "https://snapshot.debian.org/mr/timestamp/?archive=debian",
            "format": "json",
            "transformTemplates": [
                "{ \"releases\": result.debian[[-300..-1]].{ \"version\": $ } }"
            ]
        },
        // The update feed of the *arr apps (Prowlarr, Radarr, Lidarr, Sonarr:
        // the apps' updaters read it): a JSON list of releases, newest first,
        // each with its archive's sha256 (`hash`) and its GitHub download URL.
        // The URL, one per app and platform, is each dependency's `registryUrl`
        // (containers/*/docker-bake.hcl). No digest lookup: Renovate takes
        // `digest` as is.
        "servarr": {
            "format": "json",
            "transformTemplates": [
                "{ \"sourceUrl\": $substringBefore($[0].url, \"/releases/download/\"), \"releases\": [$.{ \"version\": version, \"releaseTimestamp\": releaseDate, \"digest\": hash }] }"
            ]
        },
        // The crates.io versions of a crate (RAPx: the crate is its release,
        // upstream has no git tag), each with its .crate's sha256 (`checksum`)
        // and publish date. The URL, with the crate's name, is the dependency's
        // `registryUrl` (containers/rapx/docker-bake.hcl). Not the built-in
        // `crate` datasource: it gives no digest. Yanked versions left out.
        "crates-io": {
            "format": "json",
            "transformTemplates": [
                "{ \"releases\": [versions[yanked = false].{ \"version\": num, \"releaseTimestamp\": created_at, \"digest\": checksum }] }"
            ]
        },
        // The Rust nightly a crate's release builds with (containers/rapx):
        // a rustc driver like RAPx supports the nightlies of its time, so
        // the version is the date a release was published, the nightly
        // dated that day. A nightly newer than the newest release never
        // appears: the cap that keeps RAPx and its nightly in lockstep.
        "crates-io-date": {
            "format": "json",
            "transformTemplates": [
                "{ \"releases\": [versions[yanked = false].{ \"version\": $substringBefore(created_at, \"T\"), \"releaseTimestamp\": created_at }] }"
            ]
        }
    },
    "customManagers": [
        {
            "customType": "regex",
            "description": "Cilium chart of bootc/fedora-coreos's test cluster (vm.sh cluster).",
            "managerFilePatterns": ["/^bootc/fedora-coreos/vm\\.sh$/"],
            "matchStrings": ["cilium/cilium --version (?<currentValue>\\S+)"],
            "depNameTemplate": "cilium",
            "registryUrlTemplate": "https://helm.cilium.io",
            "datasourceTemplate": "helm"
        },
        {
            "customType": "regex",
            "description": "custom-coreos-disk-images, which bootc/fedora-coreos/disk-images.sh runs: pinned to a commit of its main branch (no release).",
            "managerFilePatterns": ["/^bootc/fedora-coreos/disk-images\\.sh$/"],
            "matchStrings": ["disk_images_commit=\"(?<currentDigest>[0-9a-f]{40})\""],
            "depNameTemplate": "coreos/custom-coreos-disk-images",
            "packageNameTemplate": "https://github.com/coreos/custom-coreos-disk-images",
            "currentValueTemplate": "main",
            "datasourceTemplate": "git-refs"
        },
        {
            "customType": "regex",
            "description": "Go of the Dalec specs: their golang-<major.minor>-go build dependency, from trixie-backports, whose golang-go (version 2:<major.minor>~...) depends on the newest one. Through Repology, by source package (golang-defaults builds golang-go): the deb datasource only reads Packages.gz, and backports only publishes Packages.xz.",
            "managerFilePatterns": ["/^containers/[^/]+/spec\\.yml$/"],
            "matchStrings": ["\\bgolang-(?<currentValue>\\d+\\.\\d+)-go: "],
            "depNameTemplate": "golang-go",
            "packageNameTemplate": "debian_13_backports/golang-defaults",
            "datasourceTemplate": "repology",
            "extractVersionTemplate": "^\\d+:(?<version>\\d+\\.\\d+)~",
            "versioningTemplate": "loose"
        },
        {
            "customType": "regex",
            "description": "Every version of the application images: a `# renovate: datasource=<d> depName=<n> [packageName=] [registryUrl=] [versioning=] [extractVersion=] [depType=]` comment of a docker-bake.hcl, then the line with the version in quotes and, if any, the source's checksum (the tag's commit, one match so both change together). The comment is the whole configuration; the .github/workflows/renovate.yml extract job fails if one isn't picked up.",
            "managerFilePatterns": ["/(^|/)docker-bake\\.hcl$/"],
            "matchStrings": [
                "#[ \\t]*renovate:[ \\t]+datasource=(?<datasource>\\S+)[ \\t]+depName=(?<depName>\\S+)(?:[ \\t]+packageName=(?<packageName>\\S+))?(?:[ \\t]+registryUrl=(?<registryUrl>\\S+))?(?:[ \\t]+versioning=(?<versioning>\\S+))?(?:[ \\t]+extractVersion=(?<extractVersion>\\S+))?(?:[ \\t]+depType=(?<depType>\\S+))?[ \\t]*\\n[^\\n\"]*\"(?<currentValue>[^\"]+)\"(?:[^\\n\"]*\"(?<currentDigest>[^\"]+)\")?"
            ]
        },
        {
            "customType": "regex",
            "description": "Dalec frontend of the specs (# syntax= line, which the dockerfile manager only reads in Containerfiles).",
            "managerFilePatterns": ["/^containers/[^/]+/spec\\.yml$/"],
            "matchStrings": [
                "# syntax=(?<depName>[^:\\s]+):(?<currentValue>\\S+)"
            ],
            "datasourceTemplate": "docker",
            "versioningTemplate": "docker"
        },
        {
            "customType": "regex",
            "description": "Images run by the scripts and the commands in the docs (image-builder-cli, hadolint...).",
            "managerFilePatterns": [
                "/^containers/[^/]+/[^/]+\\.sh$/",
                "/^bootc/[^/]+\\.sh$/",
                "/\\.md$/"
            ],
            "matchStrings": [
                "(?<depName>(?:docker|ghcr|quay)\\.io/[a-z0-9._/-]+):(?<currentValue>v?\\d[\\w.-]*)"
            ],
            "datasourceTemplate": "docker",
            "versioningTemplate": "docker"
        }
    ],
    "packageRules": [
        {
            "description": "Wait 3 days before proposing a GitHub or Forgejo release or tag, a release of the *arr apps, an npm package or a crate (actions, k3s, upstream sources, Prowlarr, Radarr, Lidarr, Sonarr, configarr's pnpm, fluffychat's wasm-pack, RAPx's crate, automerged and run in a networked build step): time for a broken or malicious release to be pulled, and for CRI-O to publish the repository of a new Kubernetes minor release. Not images: Renovate only gets release dates from Docker Hub, and holds updates without one.",
            "matchDatasources": [
                "github-releases",
                "github-release-attachments",
                "github-tags",
                "forgejo-tags",
                "custom.servarr",
                "custom.crates-io",
                "custom.crates-io-date",
                "npm",
                "crate"
            ],
            "minimumReleaseAge": "3 days"
        },
        {
            "description": "GitHub Actions and runners: one PR for all, like Dependabot did, automerged once CI is green.",
            "matchManagers": ["github-actions"],
            "matchUpdateTypes": ["minor", "patch", "digest", "pin", "pinDigest"],
            "groupName": "GitHub Actions",
            "semanticCommitType": "ci",
            "automerge": true
        },
        {
            "description": "Build tools, and runtimes the image's tests run (configarr's node), that CI exercises (the Containerfiles' smoke tests, the spec's tests, test_geoblock.nu), or doc-only: automerge minor/patch once CI is green. Not digest updates (pinned FROM lines: see the weekly rule below).",
            "matchDepNames": [
                "docker.io/library/golang",
                "docker.io/library/node",
                "docker.io/library/rust",
                "golang-go",
                "ghcr.io/nushell/nushell",
                "ghcr.io/project-dalec/dalec/frontend",
                "docker.io/hadolint/hadolint",
                "ghcr.io/renovatebot/renovate",
                "docker.io/rhysd/actionlint",
                "ghcr.io/zizmorcore/zizmor"
            ],
            "matchUpdateTypes": ["minor", "patch"],
            "automerge": true
        },
        {
            "description": "Renovate's image (renovate.yml's extract job, the validator of AGENTS.md's checks): several releases a day, each its own automerged PR. Proposed in a nightly window, before 5am, so about one a day. The window is 5 hours: Mend's hosted Renovate runs a repository every 4 hours (docs/usage/mend-hosted/job-scheduling.md).",
            "matchDepNames": ["ghcr.io/renovatebot/renovate"],
            "schedule": ["* 0-4 * * *"]
        },
        {
            "description": "Application releases that CI exercises (depType=automerge in the docker-bake.hcl comment: the build stage's tests, a single-node server through the S3 API for Garage): automerge minor/patch once CI is green. Not digest updates: a moved tag. Major releases by hand: Garage's need a migration (AGENTS.md, Updates).",
            "matchDepTypes": ["automerge"],
            "matchUpdateTypes": ["minor", "patch"],
            "automerge": true
        },
        {
            "description": "Silo and pgsty/mc (depType=automerge-all): every release automerged once CI is green (the build stage tests it: Silo's runs a server through the S3 API). Major too: the versioning is by date, so a new year is a major update, not a breaking change. Not digest updates: a moved tag. The note keeps what changed in the merged PR.",
            "matchDepTypes": ["automerge-all"],
            "matchUpdateTypes": ["major", "minor", "patch"],
            "automerge": true,
            "prBodyNotes": [
                "What changed: https://github.com/{{{depName}}}/compare/{{{currentValue}}}...{{{newValue}}}"
            ]
        },
        {
            "description": "GeoLite2 databases of datalists (P3TERX/GeoLite.mmdb): a release every 3 days, deleted with its tag once two newer exist. No wait (the 3-day rule above would only ever pick a release about to be deleted), every update automerged once CI is green (the files' checksums, from Renovate's digest): an unmerged update breaks the build within about 6 days. Major too: the versioning is by date. One PR for the three files: a release's files go together.",
            "matchDepNames": ["P3TERX/GeoLite.mmdb"],
            "groupName": "GeoLite2",
            "minimumReleaseAge": null,
            "matchUpdateTypes": ["major", "minor", "patch"],
            "automerge": true
        },
        {
            "description": "NZBGet and the par2cmdline-turbo and rapidyenc tags its build names (containers/nzbget): one PR, so a new NZBGet comes with the tags it names. The spec fails while a library's newest tag is one NZBGet doesn't name yet: the PR waits for NZBGet's next release.",
            "matchDepNames": [
                "nzbgetcom/nzbget",
                "nzbgetcom/par2cmdline-turbo",
                "nzbgetcom/rapidyenc"
            ],
            "groupName": "nzbget"
        },
        {
            "description": "flux2 and the controllers of its manifests/bases/ (containers/flux-aio): one PR, so a Flux release comes with the controller tags it names. The build fails while a controller's tag is one flux2 doesn't name yet (lockstep): the PR waits for the Flux release. A controller's major release too (separateMajorMinor): alone, it fails lockstep the same way. Not containers/flux-toolbox's flux2: its own automerged PR.",
            "matchFileNames": ["containers/flux-aio/docker-bake.hcl"],
            "matchDepNames": [
                "fluxcd/flux2",
                "fluxcd/source-controller",
                "fluxcd/kustomize-controller",
                "fluxcd/helm-controller",
                "fluxcd/notification-controller",
                "fluxcd/source-watcher",
                "fluxcd/image-reflector-controller",
                "fluxcd/image-automation-controller"
            ],
            "groupName": "flux-aio",
            "separateMajorMinor": false
        },
        {
            "description": "FluffyChat and the releases its build names (containers/fluffychat): Flutter (.fvmrc), vodozemac, native_imaging and LiveKit's Flutter SDK (pubspec.lock). One PR, so a FluffyChat release comes with the releases it names. The build fails while one's newest release is one FluffyChat doesn't name yet (lockstep): the PR waits for FluffyChat's next release, and when that release names an older one, the PR is set to it by hand (containers/fluffychat/AGENTS.md, Updates). A major release too (separateMajorMinor): alone, it fails lockstep the same way.",
            "matchDepNames": [
                "krille-chan/fluffychat",
                "flutter/flutter",
                "famedly/dart-vodozemac",
                "famedly/dart_native_imaging",
                "livekit/client-sdk-flutter"
            ],
            "groupName": "fluffychat",
            "separateMajorMinor": false
        },
        {
            "description": "RAPx and the Rust nightly its build names (containers/rapx): one PR, as the nightly is the date of the RAPx release (datasource crates-io-date), so they stay in lockstep. Proposed on Saturday between midnight and 5am, like the snapshot above. A new year is a major update of the nightly (versioning by date), never automerged.",
            "matchDepNames": ["rapx", "rapx-nightly"],
            "groupName": "rapx",
            "separateMajorMinor": false,
            "schedule": ["* 0-4 * * 6"],
            "updateNotScheduled": false
        },
        {
            "description": "The application images' FROM lines carry a digest. Not the bootc images': see ignorePresets.",
            "matchManagers": ["dockerfile"],
            "matchFileNames": ["containers/**"],
            "pinDigests": true
        },
        {
            "description": "What follows Debian between two image releases, one PR on Saturday (the day before the weekly rebuild), automerged once CI is green: the archive snapshot of docker-bake.hcl, and the digests of the application images' FROM lines. Proposed between midnight and 5am, as Renovate's image above: snapshots come every few hours, so a whole-day schedule merged several each Saturday. An open PR isn't updated outside the window either (updateNotScheduled). Every rule of the group has this schedule: the group is one branch.",
            "matchDepNames": ["debian-snapshot"],
            "groupName": "Debian snapshot and base digests",
            "schedule": ["* 0-4 * * 6"],
            "updateNotScheduled": false,
            "automerge": true
        },
        {
            "description": "Digests of the application images' FROM lines: grouped with the Debian snapshot above.",
            "matchManagers": ["dockerfile"],
            "matchFileNames": ["containers/**"],
            "matchUpdateTypes": ["digest", "pin", "pinDigest"],
            "groupName": "Debian snapshot and base digests",
            "schedule": ["* 0-4 * * 6"],
            "updateNotScheduled": false,
            "automerge": true
        },
        {
            "description": "Digests of the images a docker-bake.hcl pins (the golang builders of kubectl, one per release line, which a FROM line can't vary, and of flux-aio, upstream's Go minor release): the same as the FROM lines' above.",
            "matchFileNames": ["containers/*/docker-bake.hcl"],
            "matchDatasources": ["docker"],
            "matchUpdateTypes": ["digest"],
            "groupName": "Debian snapshot and base digests",
            "schedule": ["* 0-4 * * 6"],
            "updateNotScheduled": false,
            "automerge": true
        },
        {
            "description": "The datalists digest of the lists stages (containers/haproxy, containers/cs-haproxy-spoa-bouncer): updated each time datalists is pushed, not on Saturday with the base digests above, and automerged once the smoke tests pass: haproxy's load the lists, the bouncer's looks up GeoLite2.",
            "matchDepNames": ["ghcr.io/spnngl/images/datalists"],
            "groupName": "datalists",
            "schedule": ["at any time"],
            "automerge": true
        },
        {
            "description": "CrowdSec's hub, pinned to a commit of its master branch (containers/crowdsec): several commits a day, so weekly with the snapshot above, automerged once the spec's tests (hub items installed offline) pass.",
            "matchDepNames": ["crowdsecurity/hub"],
            "groupName": "Debian snapshot and base digests",
            "schedule": ["* 0-4 * * 6"],
            "updateNotScheduled": false,
            "automerge": true
        },
        {
            "description": "Silo media server, pinned to a commit of its main branch (containers/silo-server): no release, tens of commits a day, and each PR update rebuilds the image. Proposed on Saturday between midnight and 5am, like the snapshot above, its PR not updated outside that window; merged by hand. The note keeps what changed.",
            "matchDepNames": ["Silo-Server/silo-server"],
            "schedule": ["* 0-4 * * 6"],
            "updateNotScheduled": false,
            "prBodyNotes": [
                "What changed: https://github.com/{{{depName}}}/compare/{{{currentDigest}}}...{{{newDigest}}}"
            ]
        },
        {
            "description": "MinIO and its forks (minio/minio, pgsty/silo, pgsty/mc): RELEASE.<date>T<time>Z tags. Versioning: by date then time (the seconds left out: regex versioning has five parts).",
            "matchCurrentValue": "/^RELEASE\\./",
            "versioning": "regex:^RELEASE\\.(?<major>\\d{4})-(?<minor>\\d{2})-(?<patch>\\d{2})T(?<build>\\d{2})-(?<revision>\\d{2})-\\d{2}Z$"
        },
        {
            "description": "Debian snapshots, <year><month><day>T<hour><minute><second>Z: by date, then by time.",
            "matchDepNames": ["debian-snapshot"],
            "versioning": "regex:^(?<major>\\d{4})(?<minor>\\d{2})(?<patch>\\d{2})T(?<build>\\d{2})(?<revision>\\d{4})Z$"
        },
        {
            "description": "What to do before merging an application image's update: its AGENTS.md, Updates section (a checksum-only update means the tag was moved upstream). Never automerged unless a rule above says so.",
            "matchFileNames": ["containers/*/docker-bake.hcl"],
            "prBodyNotes": [
                "Before merging, follow the *Updates* section of [`{{{packageFileDir}}}/AGENTS.md`](https://github.com/spnngl/images/blob/main/{{{packageFileDir}}}/AGENTS.md#updates). A checksum-only update means the tag was moved upstream."
            ]
        },
        {
            "description": "Mjolnir's native addons: pinned at upstream's yarn.lock versions, which the build checks (containers/mjolnir/AGENTS.md). A new release is listed on the Dependency Dashboard, the notice of what upstream will need; its PR, red until upstream's lockfile has it, only on approval.",
            "matchFileNames": ["containers/mjolnir/docker-bake.hcl"],
            "matchDepNames": ["@tensorflow/tfjs-node", "matrix-org/matrix-rust-sdk-crypto-nodejs"],
            "dependencyDashboardApproval": true
        },
        {
            "description": "k3s: automerge (k3s builds, Kubernetes patch and minor releases: there is no 2.x). A minor release fails CI until CRI-O publishes its repository (bootc/k3s/install.sh); re-run the PR's checks then. Patch releases get their own PR meanwhile.",
            "matchDepNames": ["k3s"],
            "automerge": true,
            "separateMinorPatch": true
        },
        {
            "description": "A Kubernetes minor release changes the kubeenv tags: hosts must move.",
            "matchDepNames": ["k3s"],
            "matchUpdateTypes": ["minor", "major"],
            "prBodyNotes": [
                "Merging changes the `kubeenv` tags (`-v{{{newMajor}}}.{{{newMinor}}}k3s`): `bootc upgrade` stays on the old tag, which is no longer rebuilt. Move hosts with `bootc switch`."
            ]
        },
        {
            "description": "Base images: never automerged, a new major release changes the image tag. CI fails until its sysroot/<BASE_VERSION>/ (policy.json) is added: bootc/fedora/policy.jq.",
            "matchDepNames": [
                "quay.io/fedora/fedora-bootc",
                "quay.io/almalinuxorg/almalinux-bootc"
            ],
            "prBodyNotes": [
                "Before merging, add `bootc/<name>/sysroot/{{{newValue}}}/` (from `{{{currentValue}}}/`, removed if no build uses it any more) with the new base's `/etc/containers/policy.json` plus our changes (bootc/REFERENCES.md, \"Signing\"). CI fails until then. What changed in the base's file:\n\n```sh\ndiff <(podman run --rm {{{depName}}}:{{{currentValue}}} cat /etc/containers/policy.json) <(podman run --rm {{{depName}}}:{{{newValue}}} cat /etc/containers/policy.json)\n```\n\nMerging changes the image tag: move hosts with `bootc switch`."
            ]
        },
        {
            "description": "Fedora releases from endoflife.date, not from the image's tags: quay.io/fedora/fedora-bootc tags the branched release and rawhide with their number months before release.",
            "matchDepNames": ["quay.io/fedora/fedora-bootc"],
            "overrideDatasource": "endoflife-date",
            "overridePackageName": "fedora"
        },
        {
            "description": "Fedora CoreOS: the stable stream's releases only (<major>.<date>.3.<n>); its tags also hold the testing (.2.) and next (.1.) streams.",
            "matchDepNames": ["quay.io/fedora/fedora-coreos"],
            "allowedVersions": "/^\\d+\\.\\d{8}\\.3\\.\\d+$/"
        },
        {
            "description": "A new Fedora major of fedora-coreos: the GPU image's NVIDIA repository URLs hold it (bootc/fedora-coreos/nvidia.repo takes it from the base, $releasever, but the driver's registryUrl in docker-bake.hcl is literal).",
            "matchDepNames": ["quay.io/fedora/fedora-coreos"],
            "matchUpdateTypes": ["major"],
            "prBodyNotes": [
                "Change `fedora<major>` in the `registryUrl=` of the `NVIDIA_DRIVER` comment of `bootc/fedora-coreos/docker-bake.hcl` to the new major, and check that NVIDIA's repository for it holds an R620 driver (`bootc/fedora-coreos/REFERENCES.md`, \"GPU image\")."
            ]
        },
        {
            "description": "NVIDIA's driver of the GPU image: the R620 branch (long-term support until September 2029) only; a new branch changes the kernel module and the CUDA the nodes' workloads run against. Its PR is never automerged (the rule for bootc/fedora-coreos below), and the toolkit's: the node's GPUs and the operator's pods depend on them.",
            "matchDepNames": ["nvidia-driver"],
            "allowedVersions": "/^620\\./"
        },
        {
            "description": "custom-coreos-disk-images, pinned to a commit of its main branch: weekly, on Saturday between midnight and 5am like the pins above. The note keeps what changed.",
            "matchDepNames": ["coreos/custom-coreos-disk-images"],
            "schedule": ["* 0-4 * * 6"],
            "updateNotScheduled": false,
            "prBodyNotes": [
                "What changed: https://github.com/{{{depName}}}/compare/{{{currentDigest}}}...{{{newDigest}}}"
            ]
        },
        {
            "description": "bootc/fedora-coreos: CI builds and scans it, and its vm-test job runs the VM tests (bootc/fedora-coreos/AGENTS.md, Build check). Not automerged, but for the rules below.",
            "matchFileNames": ["bootc/fedora-coreos/**"],
            "automerge": false,
            "prBodyNotes": [
                "CI builds and scans it, and its `vm-test` job runs the build check of [`bootc/fedora-coreos/AGENTS.md`](https://github.com/spnngl/images/blob/main/bootc/fedora-coreos/AGENTS.md#build-check) on the image. A Fedora CoreOS release or Kubernetes patch keeps the image's tag (`<major>-v<minor>`): nodes take it with `bootc upgrade`. A new major or Kubernetes minor is a new tag: VMs get new machines through Cluster API, dedicated servers move with `bootc switch`."
            ]
        },
        {
            "description": "Fedora CoreOS releases of the same major (BASE_VERSION <major>.<date>.3.<n>: docker versioning makes the date the minor): automerged once every check is green, build-bootc's gate-bootc check included; the tag stays, so nodes take them with `bootc upgrade`. A new major changes the tag: by hand.",
            "matchDepNames": ["quay.io/fedora/fedora-coreos"],
            "matchUpdateTypes": ["minor", "patch"],
            "automerge": true
        },
        {
            "description": "Kubernetes patch releases of bootc/fedora-coreos, one dependency per line (kubernetes-<major.minor>, whose extractVersion keeps its line): automerged as the rule above, once every check is green, the vm-test job's included; the tag stays. A new line is a new tag: added by hand (bootc/fedora-coreos/AGENTS.md, \"Kubernetes lines\").",
            "matchDepNames": ["/^kubernetes-\\d+\\.\\d+$/"],
            "matchUpdateTypes": ["patch"],
            "automerge": true
        },
        {
            "description": "What only the vm-test job of bootc/fedora-coreos runs, automerged as the rules above: the test cluster's Cilium chart (vm.sh cluster; a major release by hand), and custom-coreos-disk-images (the qemu disk image the job boots; the release job's OpenStack one runs no test).",
            "matchDepNames": ["cilium", "coreos/custom-coreos-disk-images"],
            "matchUpdateTypes": ["minor", "patch", "digest"],
            "automerge": true
        },
        {
